    "name": "2.2 Purpose",
    "text": "7 purpose. — “the trust is established ‘for. the “exélusive purgese \"26 providing, certain pension. ‘and ‘related | benefits. ‘to Covered. Employees. under the. Plan, and, shall further provide the means for. financing | and maintaining ‘the: operation and - administration of the Trust. and Plan in accordance with. this Agreenent, the Plan, and applicable law."
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "2.3 Operation",
    "text": "2. 3. ‘Operation.. It. is. intended that. this Prust shall be established ‘and operated in a manner that. shall qualify it as an organization exempt from income taxation in. accordance. with Section 501(a). of. the. Code. | Notwithstanding anything. ‘to the | a contrary contained herein, the Trust: shall be operated . exclusive-. ly for such. purposes. as- will. compl ith. section 401 (a). and 501(a) .of.. the Code, . and. to the extent. that anything. herein is inconsistent ‘therewith, ‘this. Agreement. shall be. deemed. amended. in such fashion as will implement the purposes of this Trust while | continuing. to comply. with the. requirements of. the. Code. Tt is further. intended tha this ‘Trust. shall be. established. and. operated. in. a manner that ‘complies | with, ERISA. To. the extent. ‘that anything, herein, is. inconsistent with. ERISA, this a Agreement | shall. be: deemed amended in such. fashion as. wild imple- ‘ment the purposes of this Trust while continuing to comply with the requirements of ERISA. ree “The Trust shall. also be. ‘established and ‘operated, as. a. \"jointly-administered\". ‘pension: fund | within the meaning of, and in accordance with, Section 302(c) of ‘the ‘Labor “Management. Relations Act of 1947, as amended."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "2.4 Participation by Contributing Employers",
    "text": "a 2.4 ‘participation. by. Contributing Employers. Any . contributing Employer acceptable to the Trustees may participate in the Trust and the Plan by: (a) executing a copy of. a Collective: Bar- . - gaining Agreement ‘approved. by. the. Board. requiring contributions to be made by such Employer to the Fund; (b) designating a date on which such participation shall become effective; and (c) designating the categories of employment of Covered Employees to participate in such Plan."
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "2.5 Obligations of Contributing Employers",
    "text": "2.5 Obligations of Contributing Employers. An Employer shall be deemed to have: (a) (b) (c) (a) reviewed, understood and adopted the Trust and all provisions of this Agreement and the Plan which it establishes hereunder (and any amendments to such Agreement or Plan); agreed to be bound unconditionally to said Plan and Trust, as well as all of the decisions of the Trustees appointed pursuant hereto; agreed to be bound unconditionally to the provisions of the Plan and all amendments thereto; and agreed to pay the costs of the Plan applicable to its Covered Employees by means of periodic contributions as set forth in the Plan, a Collective Bargaining Agreement, or other document, or as may be required by law."
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "3.1 Composition of Trustees",
    "text": "3.2: “composition of: Trustees. “The. Trustees under this Agreement, who shall be Trustees of' of the Trust created and established hereunder, shall be two. (2). ‘Employer. Trustees, who shall be selected by the Association, and three’(3) Union Trustees, who shall be selected by the Union. The appointment of Trustees shall be governed by the provisions of Section 3.4."
  },
  {
    "id": "c040",
    "name": "3.2 Acceptance of Trust and Trusteeship",
    "text": "3.2 Acceptance: of Trust and ‘Trusteeship. The Trustees appointed hereunder hereby accept the Trust created and established by this Agreement and consent to act as Trustees thereof by assuming the: responsibility for the operation and administration of the’ Trust.” By. their® sigriature to this Agree~ ment, or any counterpart or: ‘COpy: hereof, each Trustee hereby agrees to accept the trusteeship and to act in their capacities as trustees and fiduciaries of. the: Trust’ Fund in accordance with the provisions of this: Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c041",
    "name": "3.3 Selection of Trustees",
    "text": "3. 3 ‘Selection of. mouataaa, (a a)~ ‘The Trustees currently designated by the Association are: BARBARA KALISH and ROBERT NUSSPICKLE. . (b) The Trustees currently designated by the Union are: FRANK SPARACINO, PATRICK LAGAN and JOSEPH COTTER."
  },
  {
    "id": "c042",
    "name": "3.4 Written Appointments and Acceptances",
    "text": "3.4 Written Appointments and Acceptances. Except for the appointments of the Trustees set forth in Section 3.3 of this Agreement, copies of the written appointments of. successor Trustees shall be provided to the Board as soon as practicable after the appointments. Each Trustee shall signify his acceptance of the trusteeship in writing."
  },
  {
    "id": "c043",
    "name": "3.5 Term of Office",
    "text": "3.5 Term of Office. Each Trustee appointed under this Agreement shall continue to serve as such until his death, incapacity, resignation or removal as herein provided."
  },
  {
    "id": "c044",
    "name": "3.6 Resignations",
    "text": "3.6 Resiqnations. A Trustee may resign, and shall be fully discharged (to the extent permitted by law) from further duty or responsibility hereunder, upon giving at least fifteen (15) days advance written notice to the Board (and to the Contributing Employer | that designated him as a Trustee), or such shorter notice as the Board may accept as sufficient, in which notice there shall be stated a date when such resignation shall take effect; and such resignation shall take effect on the date specified in the notice, unless a successor Trustee shall have been appointed (as provided by Section 3.9 or Section 3.10) at an earlier date, in which event such resignation shall take effect immediately upon the successor Trustee taking office. A Trustee shall be deemed to have resigned and shall not be replaced in the 9 FUND0002285 bis ‘ event that the Contributing Employer which designated him shall cease to be a Contributing Employer hereunder."
  },
  {
    "id": "c045",
    "name": "3.7 Removal of Employer Trustees",
    "text": "3.7 Removal of Employer Trustees. Any Employer Trustee may be removed from office at any time, with or without cause, by instrument in writing, signed by a duly authorized officer of the Association, filed with the Board, and shall become effective immediately upon such filing."
  },
  {
    "id": "c046",
    "name": "3.8 Removal of Union Trustees",
    "text": "3.8 Removal of Union Trustees. The Union Trustees shall be the incumbent president, vice president and secretarytreasurer of the Union. Those persons shall serve as Union Trustees unless prevented from doing so by operation of applicable law, in which case a Successor Union Trustee shall be elected from the full-time officers of the Union. Should any Union Trustee be removed from office by operation of law, notice thereof shall be filed with the Board by an instrument in writing signed by the principal officer of the Union, and shall become effective immediately upon such filing."
  },
  {
    "id": "c047",
    "name": "3.9 Successor Employer Trustees",
    "text": "3.9 Successor Employer Trustees. In the event any Employer Trustee shall die, become incapable of acting hereunder, resign, or be removed, a successor Employer Trustee shall be designated by filing with the Board a certificate in writing signed by a duly authorized officer of the Association."
  },
  {
    "id": "c048",
    "name": "3.10 Successor Union Trustees",
    "text": "3.10 Successor Union Trustees. In the event any Union Trustee shall die, become incapable of acting hereunder, resign or be removed, the principal officer of the Union shall designate a successor Union Trustee by filing with the Board a certification in writing signed by a duly authorized officer of the Union, in which case a Successor Union Trustee shall be elected from the full-time officers of the Union."
  },
  {
    "id": "c049",
    "name": "3.11 Powers of Successor Trustees",
    "text": "3.11 Powers of Successor Trustees. Any successor Trustee under this Agreement shall immediately, upon his designation as a successor Trustee and his acceptance of the trusteeship in writing filed with the Board, become vested with all rights, powers, privileges and duties of a Trustee hereunder with like effect as if originally named as Trustee."
  },
  {
    "id": "c050",
    "name": "3.12 Use of Corporate Trustee",
    "text": "3.12 Use of Corporate Trustee, (a) At any time and from time to time, the Board may appoint, as a Corporate Trustee, a bank or trust company located within the United States. (ob) The Board may delegate to the Corporate Trustee (i) the power to hold the Fund as sole trustee of a trust separate from the Fund created by this Trust Agreement (and not as. an agent of the Trustees or as co-trustee hereunder with the Trustees); (ii) the power to invest and reinvest the Fund in the 10 FUND0002286 wg 4 Corporate Trustee’s sole discretion; and (iii) such other duties and powers as the Board may deem, advisable, (c) The Board may: enter into and execute a trust oer custodial agreement with the: Corporate Trustee, which | agreement. shall contain such’ provisiol s. the. Board | may. deem advisable. © ‘Upon execution of: a trust agreement. with the « Corporate’ Trustee,” the Board may transfer and convey to the Corporate Trustee any part or all of the” Securities or other | property of the Fund acceptable to the. Corporate Trustee, and thereupon, ‘the Trustees shall” be» forever released and discharged from any responsibility. or liability with respect to such assets so transferred as.to any period: subsequent. to such’ transfer andwith respect to the investment and> reinvestment thereof by the Corporate Trustee. Notwithstanding such, transfer, . the. Board . functions ‘under the Plan in: “accordance with ‘the provisions. of the Plan’ and this. Agreement. ae _ | . (a) The Board: may; at any’ “time, remove the Corporate Trustee in the manner provided | in the trust. agreement between the Board and the Corporate Trustee. — In the event | that a Corporate: ‘Trustee’ is: appointed, such Corporate. Trustée shall, Lt and when. removed by the Board, ca he. transferred ‘to’ the _ Board any Trust’ Fund: ‘Securities or other. property or records. ‘then in its possession, along with a final accounting of the Securities or other property of the Fund held and/or managed by the Corporate’ Trustee pursuant to said agreement. . ae"
  },
  {
    "id": "c051",
    "name": "4.1 Benefits",
    "text": "4.1 Benefits. (a) The Board shall have full authority to determine all questions of the nature, type, form, amount and duration of benefits (including, without limitation, matters pertaining to the interpretation and application of reciprocity and portability agreements with other funds and plans) to be provided to Covered Employees and their Beneficiaries. However, no benefits other than pension, retirement, and such other related benefits as the Board may from time to time determine, -Iay be provided to Covered Employees and Beneficiaries or paid for under the Trust. (b) Payment of benefits under the Plan shall be ~~\" made directly from the Fund by the Board or may be provided for by the purchase and delivery of such insurance contracts, policies or certificates, to such persons, in such manner, and at — such time as the Plan shall provide. The Board shall be fully protected in making, discontinuing or withholding benefit pay- | ments from the Fund, or purchasing or délivering insurance contracts, policies or certificates (or instructing the insurers with respect thereto), all in reliance upon information received from the Contributing Employer respecting: the status of any Covered Employee. When any benefit payment, or the purchase or delivery of any insurance contract, policy or certificate (or any payment thereunder) is to be made in accordance with the terms of the Plan only during or until the time the person entitled to receive such benefit maintains or attains a given age or status, or only during or until the time a certain condition exists regarding» such person, any such payment, purchase, delivery or instruction made, discontinued or withheld by the Trustees in good faith, without actual knowledge or notice of the prescribed change in the age, status or condition of the payee, shall be considered to have been properly effected by the Board. (c) Each Contributing Employer shall indemnify and hold harmless the Fund and each Trustee from the consequences of relying on any information or directions furnished to the Board, the Administrator, or their agents by such Contributing Employer."
  },
  {
    "id": "c052",
    "name": "4.2 Written Plan of Benefits",
    "text": "4.2 Written Plan of Benefits. The specific detailed basis upon which eligibility for benefits, types and forms of benefits payable, and payment of benefits is to be made to Covered Employees and Beneficiaries shall be set forth in the Plan. The Board may amend or otherwise modify the Plan (from time to time) or terminate the Plan (at any time)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c053",
    "name": "4.3 Insurance Contracts",
    "text": "4.3 Insurance Contracts.:..The written plan of benefits comprising the Plan may (but need not necessarily) consist, in whole or in part, of contracts: with‘ one or more insurance companies."
  },
  {
    "id": "c054",
    "name": "4.4 Exclusive Benefit",
    "text": "4.4 Exclusive Benefit. If any Employer contribution to the Trust’ Fund has been (a) made by a mistake of fact or law, (b) the Plan status receives an. adverse determination with .... respect to its tax status qualification under Sections 401 or 501 under Section 404 of the Code; .and all. or a part.of such deduc~ - tion has been disallowed; then:the,Board may,-in.its sole discretion, return such contribution (or.the value.thereof, if . less) to the Employer prior to the expiration of (1) six.months - after a determination by: the. Administrator as.to (a).above, (2) one year following the adverse determination under. (b)..above,. or. (3) the disallowance of the deduction under (c) above (but only © to the.extent of the disallowance). 9= sss 6 os: . of the Code; or (c). conditioned upon’ the. deductibility thereof."
  },
  {
